# E-commerce Cart
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: E-commerce — a mutable pre-commit document, freely edited with none of an
# Order's invariants enforced, until Checkout converts it into a real Order
# Case 15 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
# References: ecommerce-product.menata, ecommerce-order.menata, ecommerce-cart-item.menata
#
# THE NEW FINDING THIS CASE EXISTS TO SURFACE: every "document" case so far (Case 9's
# Journal Entry, Case 14's Loan Application) treats even its Draft state as a real,
# constrained record. A Cart is scratch state — items freely added, removed, and
# re-quantified with no stock check, no minimum, no required fields at all — until
# Checkout, which is the actual commit point. No capability distinguishes "editable
# scratch state" from "Draft" (a real but not-yet-finalized record). This applies to
# Cart itself, not to how its items are modeled: those are Cart Item, a separate
# Object referencing back to this one (see ecommerce-cart-item.menata) — the ordinary
# Object References pattern, no "Items" field declared here.

Cart

Fields

- Customer : User
- Status : Open | Checked Out

Events

When Checkout

    Create Order

    Status Checked Out

Permissions

Customer

- Add Item
- Remove Item
- Checkout

Views

- My Cart : Detail
